l@870ce8b/content/data/versions/652.json", "paragraphs": ["HomeView starts at $299 and ships next month. It has a 7-inch screen and face recognition. You can hang it on a wall or put it on a table. It helps you control doorbells, thermostats and smart locks.", "The device shows Apple's new Siri AI. Apple says this Siri is more capable and conversational. It uses your messages and calendar to give better answers. Preorders start today, and the device comes out on 13 November.", "Apple also updated its HomePod speaker and Apple TV. It introduced new accessories from LG and Schneider Electric, like cameras, doorbells and a smart lock. You can manage everything in the Apple home app.", "HomeView will not be sold in the European Union. Apple says Siri AI is not available there because of EU rules. Apple faces competition from Amazon, Google and new AI companies like OpenAI."], "paragraphs_zh": ["HomeView 起价 299 美元，下个月开始发货。它有一块 7 英寸屏幕，还能识别人脸。你可以把它挂在墙上，也可以放在桌上。它能帮你控制门铃、恒温器和智能锁。", "这款设备展示了苹果新的 Siri AI。苹果说新 Siri 能力更强，更像在聊天。它会参考你的信息和日历来给出更好的回答。今天开始预订，11 月 13 日正式发售。", "苹果还更新了 HomePod 音箱和 Apple TV。它推出了 LG 和施耐德电气的新配件，比如摄像头、门铃和智能锁。你可以在苹果家庭 App 里管理所有东西。", "HomeView 不会在欧盟销售。苹果说，因为欧盟的规定，Siri AI 在那里用不了。苹果面临亚马逊、谷歌以及 OpenAI 等新 AI 公司的竞争。"], "body": "HomeView starts at $299 and ships next month. It has a 7-inch screen and face recognition. You can hang it on a wall or put it on a table. It helps you control doorbells, thermostats and smart locks.\n\nThe device shows Apple's new Siri AI. Apple says this Siri is more capable and conversational. It uses your messages and calendar to give better answers. Preorders start today, and the device comes out on 13 November.\n\nApple also updated its HomePod speaker and Apple TV. It introduced new accessories from LG and Schneider Electric, like cameras, doorbells and a smart lock. You can manage everything in the Apple home app.\n\nHomeView will not be sold in the European Union. Apple says Siri AI is not available there because of EU rules. Apple faces competition from Amazon, Google and new AI companies like OpenAI.", "body_zh": "HomeView 起价 299 美元，下个月开始发货。它有一块 7 英寸屏幕，还能识别人脸。你可以把它挂在墙上，也可以放在桌上。它能帮你控制门铃、恒温器和智能锁。\n\n这款设备展示了苹果新的 Siri AI。苹果说新 Siri 能力更强，更像在聊天。它会参考你的信息和日历来给出更好的回答。今天开始预订，11 月 13 日正式发售。\n\n苹果还更新了 HomePod 音箱和 Apple TV。它推出了 LG 和施耐德电气的新配件，比如摄像头、门铃和智能锁。你可以在苹果家庭 App 里管理所有东西。\n\nHomeView 不会在欧盟销售。苹果说，因为欧盟的规定，Siri AI 在那里用不了。苹果面临亚马逊、谷歌以及 OpenAI 等新 AI 公司的竞争。", "text": "HomeView starts at $299 and ships next month. It has a 7-inch screen and face recognition. You can hang it on a wall or put it on a table. It helps you control doorbells, thermostats and smart locks. The device shows Apple's new Siri AI. Apple says this Siri is more capable and conversational. It uses your messages and calendar to give better answers. Preorders start today, and the device comes out on 13 November. Apple also updated its HomePod speaker and Apple TV. It introduced new accessories from LG and Schneider Electric, like cameras, doorbells and a smart lock. You can manage everything in the Apple home app. HomeView will not be sold in the European Union. Apple says Siri AI is not available there because of EU rules. Apple faces competition from Amazon, Google and new AI companies like OpenAI.", "vocab": [{"word": "device", "pos": "noun", "zh": "设备", "note": "常用词，指手机、平板等电子设备", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "smart home", "pos": "phrase", "zh": "智能家居", "note": "指能用手机控制的家庭设备", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "screen", "pos": "noun", "zh": "屏幕", "note": "手机、平板、电视上显示画面的部分", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "control", "pos": "verb", "zh": "控制", "note": "常用动词，如 control the lights", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "preorder", "pos": "noun", "zh": "预订", "note": "产品上市前先下单购买", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "accessory", "pos": "noun", "zh": "配件", "note": "如摄像头、门铃等附加设备", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "available", "pos": "adj", "zh": "可用的；能买到的", "note": "常用形容词，如 not available", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "competition", "pos": "noun", "zh": "竞争", "note": "商业中公司之间的竞争", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}], "title_original": "Apple unveils new smart home devices that showcase upgraded Siri AI", "summary_original": "New products from Apple include the HomeView, an iPad-like device that acts as a hub for other smart home gadgets\nApple on Tuesday began showing off a ⁠new round of smart home products, including an iPad-like device dubbed the HomeView, meant to hang on walls or perch on tabletops ⁠and act as a hub for other smart home devices.\nThe HomeView device starts at $299 and will begin shipping next month. It will feature a 7in screen and face recognition, will help users ⁠control doorbells, thermostats and smart locks in a market where Apple has tinkered for a decade without major success. The device will also showcase Apple’s AI-upgraded Siri virtual ​assistant.\nContinue reading...", "body_original": "Apple unveils new smart home devices that showcase upgraded Siri AI\nNew products from Apple include the HomeView, an iPad-like device that acts as a hub for other smart home gadgets\nApple on Tuesday began showing off a ⁠new round of smart home products, including an iPad-like device dubbed the HomeView, meant to hang on walls or perch on tabletops ⁠and act as a hub for other smart home devices.\nThe HomeView device starts at $299 and will begin shipping next month. It will feature a 7in screen and face recognition, will help users ⁠control doorbells, thermostats and smart locks in a market where Apple has tinkered for a decade without major success. The device will also showcase Apple’s AI-upgraded Siri virtual ​assistant.\nPreorders begin today and the devices are expected to be available starting 13 November.\nApple is launching these products as it ⁠tries to fend off competition from rivals, including traditional competitors like Amazon – which has invested heavily in ​its Echo speakers and Ring doorbells and ‌last week launched premium tablets – as well as newer AI upstarts like OpenAI that have hardware ambitions of their own.\nApple’s HomeView launch was accompanied by updates to its HomePod smart speaker and Apple TV devices. It also introduced a range of ‌accessories, including doorbells, cameras and thermostats, made by LG and Schneider Electric and designed with help from Apple.\nThe new line of devices are accessible and managed in the Apple home app. The accessories include a Schneider smart thermostat and LG home security devices including indoor and various outdoor cameras including a doorbell camera and floodlight camera as well as a smart lock. The lock can be unlocked using the Apple home app.\nThe HomeView device will not be sold in the European Union, because Siri AI remains unavailable there due to EU regulations, Apple said.\nApple first released its Home app to control smart gadgets in 2016, ⁠with HomePod smart speakers following in 2018, but those offerings are competing with ​Alphabet’s Google Home speakers and ​Amazon’s Echo line. Analysts said ​two major hurdles for Apple were making its devices work with a ​variety of third-party gadgets and ‌the limited ability ​of Siri to ​give useful answers.\nThe HomeView device includes a revamped version of Siri AI, the company announced. An Apple press release described the new version of Siri as more capable and conversational, using information from personal apps like Messages and Calendar to provide more relevant answers.\n“It’s powered by Apple Intelligence with Siri AI at its core, drawing on personal context from your iPhone to help you find what you need and get more done, all while keeping everyone’s information private and secure,” the release said.\nExplore more on these topics\nApple\nAI (artificial intelligence)\nnews\nShare\nReuse this content", "fetched_at": "2026-10-14T00:29:58.101334", "timeline": [{"i": 0, "w": "HomeView", "s": 0.275, "e": 0.625, "sm": 275, "em": 625, "cs": 0, "ce": 8, "si": 0}, {"i": 1, "w": "starts", "s": 0.625, "e": 0.963, "sm": 625, "em